dialogue tavernkeeper
  node root marta "Clerk! Here for a drink, or here to inspect my shelves like it's a customs raid?"
    > "What's everyone celebrating?" -> marrow
    # One of these fills the second slot, depending on how far along we are.
    > "I need a favour." if not knows_key and not marta_paid -> favour
    > "Bramwick says you have his drawer key." if knows_key and not marta_paid -> key
    > "Thanks again for the key." if marta_paid -> thanks
    > "Bramwick still owes you a game of cards." if seen_iou and marta_paid -> iou
    > "Nothing. Goodnight." -> bye
  node marrow marta "The Marrow sails for the Straits at dawn. Half this room is drinking to a safe voyage. The other half is betting against one, and drinking faster."
    > "Ships keep vanishing out there." -> straits
    > "Who sails on her?" -> crew
    > "Goodnight, Marta." -> bye
  node crew marta "Vane, who could out-stare a gull. Hobb, the bosun, who has more names on his arms than I have on my slate. And a lookout who can spot a lie at two miles and a compliment at none."
    -> crew2
  node crew2 marta "Mind her. She bites, and she's usually right. Those two together are very hard to argue with."
    > "Ships keep vanishing out there." -> straits
    > "I'll mind her. Goodnight." -> bye
  node iou marta "Thirty years he's owed me that game. He'll never pay it. Paying would mean it's over."
    -> iou2
  node iou2 marta "…Don't you dare tell him I said that. I'll water your punch till it's a moral lesson."
    > "Your secret's safe. I'm a civil servant." -> bye
    > "He keeps it in the drawer with the stamp. Right at the front." -> front
  node front marta "Does he. …Get out of my tavern, clerk, before I start liking you."
  node straits marta "Six ships in three years. Your father's was the first. They find the hulls drifting, sails set, nobody aboard. Not so much as a cat. You're not thinking of signing on? …You are. He had that exact look."
    > "Goodnight, Marta." -> bye
  node favour marta "A clerk asking favours after the bell. Come back when you know what you want, and bring something sour. My punch is as flat as a ledger."
    > "Something sour. Noted." -> bye
  node key marta "Won it off him at cards. He bet it on a pair of threes, the old fool. It's yours in trade. My punch is as flat as a ledger tonight. Bring me a lemon."
    > "I've got one right here." if has lemon -> traded
      take lemon
      give drawer_key
      set marta_paid
      sound pickup
    > "One lemon. Done." if not has lemon -> bye
    > "Where do I find a lemon at this hour?" if not has lemon -> nolemon
  node nolemon marta "There's a crate on the pier for the Marrow's galley. Packed so tight you'd want a crowbar to get one out. Pirates pack the way they plunder."
    > "A crowbar. Noted." -> bye
  node traded marta "A lemon! The punch lives. Here's his key. And tell him a pair of threes is not a strategy."
    > "Goodnight, Marta." -> bye
  node thanks marta "Thank the lemon. And Fenn: whatever's out in those Straits, come back and tell me. I hate an unfinished story."
    > "I will." -> bye
  node bye marta "Mind the step. It's been drinking too."
